+
+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` accepts `{ "csv": "..." }` with header
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`. Tickets are nonempty strings, dish ids and quantities
+  are positive integers, and `soldAt` is an ISO instant with a timezone. Each
+  quantity uses that many portions of the dish's recipe. Returns
+  `{ "tickets": 1, "dishes": 2 }`, counting new tickets and portions sold.
+  Previously imported tickets are skipped. All rows must be valid; an invalid
+  row or stock shortage rejects the whole file with a row-numbered error
+  (the first data row is row 2). Consumption uses `sale:<ticket>` as its ref
+  and the sale instant as its time.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 0.6, "actual": 0.8, "variance": 0.2 }`.
+  Dates are required, inclusive UTC days, with `from` on or before `to`.
+  Theoretical use is the saved recipe ingredient quantities for sales in the
+  range; actual use includes every consume movement in the range. Variance is
+  actual minus theoretical, in the item's unit. Only items with positive use
+  in either column are included, ordered by item id.
